# Left from the layout where `main.py` sat here and this directory was the
# thing deployed. The deployable units are the `examples/*` directories
# now, and each is uploaded on its own, so this file only matters if you
# build from here. Kept because the exclusions are still the right ones and
# the reasoning is worth not rediscovering: the suite, its fixtures and its
# caches are not part of any service, and uploading them makes a slower
# build and a larger image for no benefit.
.git/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.mypy_cache/
test/
requirements-dev.txt
live/
examples/

# An example deployed from its own directory uploads that directory alone:
# its `main.py`, its `requirements.txt`, and whatever else it is made of.
# The package arrives as an install, exactly as it would for a user.
